Each of these requirements carries financial 
implications. Yet the findings suggest that 
financial flexibility has not evolved at the same 
pace as regulatory expectations. The result 
is what may be described as a sustainability 
gap. Schools face increasing obligations while 
operating within frameworks that provide 
relatively limited support for generating the 
resources necessary to fulfil those obligations. 
This tension appears repeatedly throughout the 
regulatory architecture.
FINDING 5 
Sustainability Is a Public Interest Issue
Discussions on financial sustainability are 
often framed as matters affecting school 
operators alone. The findings suggest a 
broader perspective is required. Institutional 
sustainability directly affects:
• educational continuity;
• teacher retention;
• infrastructure quality;
• organisational resilience;
